WEBVTT

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:00.025
Because they had grown up
in a different situation.

00:10:00.049 --> 00:10:04.071
They had grown up with certain kinds
of values infused into them,

00:10:04.095 --> 00:10:05.858
which were kind of taken for granted.

00:10:05.882 --> 00:10:09.404
And it was actually -- you could
throw off a lot of the rules,

00:10:09.428 --> 00:10:11.741
but still, they believed in love.

00:10:11.765 --> 00:10:14.097
They believed in connection
with each other.

00:10:14.121 --> 00:10:16.839
They just didn't want
to be told how to do it.

00:10:16.863 --> 00:10:20.924
Is it possible that that generation
actually did OK, but that what went wrong

00:10:20.948 --> 00:10:23.276
was that the kids that they raised

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:27.414
were all raised not to think about,
really, communal responsibility

00:10:27.438 --> 00:10:29.986
but just about their own
preciousness and specialness